 "observations": [
  "body (table): the top of the frame is printed as a double rule (heavy and thin), the rule under the heads as a heavy rule; the rules above and below «Crater» are thin, the lower one printed in short pieces; the outer vertical rules are double (heavy outside); the foot of the frame is a double rule (thin and heavy).",
  "body (table): a speck is printed under «descriptio» in the head; not transcribed. The final e of «prope» (Hydra 10), the r of the first «Hydrae» and the first t of «capitis» (Hydra 12) are printed broken.",
  "body (notes): the two dots of qāf are printed merged into a short stroke in «قعد», «قعر», «قنج» and «قيج», those of yāʾ in «قيج» and «يو».",
  "body (note 9): «قعر» (177) is printed with the zāy without its dot.",
  "body (note 11): «dóes» is printed so, with an accented o.",
  "body (note 13): «Hg» is printed without a period before the comma; in «ιϛ̄» and «ιϛ̄′» the sign after the iota is printed as a stigma with a stroke at its top right (transcribed ϛ̄, as on p. 272), the second followed by a prime; «there to» is printed in two words.",
  "body (Crater, note 3): «Escu» is printed without a hyphen at the end of the line."
